---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import PromptTemplateLibrary from '../../components/PromptTemplateLibrary.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Prompt Template Library"
  description="Ready-to-use prompt templates for summarization, extraction, code review, classification, and more — copy and fill in the blanks."
>
  <PromptTemplateLibrary client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why use a template instead of writing from scratch</h2>
  <p>
    Well-structured prompts consistently produce better, more predictable
    results than ad-hoc phrasing — especially for tasks like extraction or
    classification where you need a specific output format. These templates
    are starting points, tested patterns you can adapt to your exact use case.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use these templates</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Browse by category or search the list.</li>
    <li>Copy the template that matches your task.</li>
    <li>Replace each <code>{"{placeholder}"}</code> with your actual content.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Prompt Template Library FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Do these work with any AI model?</strong> Yes — these are
    general-purpose prompt patterns that work across GPT, Claude, Gemini,
    and other instruction-following models.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Can I request a new template?</strong> Yes, reach out via the
    contact page with the task you're trying to solve.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
